WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:08.470
Every FPS player wishes they were an aim-god,
but very few people ever reach that status.

00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:12.050
But what does it take to make that happen?

00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:14.940
Does it rely on good genetics?

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:21.720
Or are there advanced tactics for improving
aim that can help anyone achieve insane aiming

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:22.720
skills?

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:28.930
Well, when asking myself these sorts of questions,
I thought of no-one better to answer them

00:00:28.930 --> 00:00:33.079
than the FPS Coach himself, Ron "Rambo" Kim.

00:00:33.079 --> 00:00:38.309
After years of playing Counter-Strike professionally,
followed by years of coaching top teams like

00:00:38.309 --> 00:00:46.710
Complexity and Cloud 9, Ron has accumulated
a wealth of FPS knowledge &amp; aiming skill.

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:52.489
And so, by defining key aspects of aiming,
teaching you the mindset needed to improve,

00:00:52.489 --> 00:00:58.659
and implementing an advanced perspective on
how to play at your maximum ability, you might

00:00:58.659 --> 00:01:04.860
just end up on the fast-track to developing
insane aiming skills and getting one step

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:10.420
close to the status of an aim-god.

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:18.369
Before diving too far into the principles
for improving your aim, it's important to

00:01:18.369 --> 00:01:25.359
note that aim is only one of several vital
aspects when it comes to FPS skills, and any

00:01:25.359 --> 00:01:29.289
good FPS coach, including Ron, will tell you
this.

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:35.909
Basically, aim mechanics alone can't carry
you to the top; you need to combine it with

00:01:35.909 --> 00:01:40.609
great gamesense and positioning to unlock
it's potential.

00:01:40.609 --> 00:01:47.119
Fortunately, having better aim can help you
improve these other aspects much faster.

00:01:47.119 --> 00:01:51.869
The more you can rely on your aim, the less
you'll need to focus on it, and the more free

00:01:51.869 --> 00:01:56.860
your mind will be to focus on the other aspects
of the match.

00:01:56.860 --> 00:02:01.759
And as you become more confident and consistent
with your aim, you'll become far more confident

00:02:01.759 --> 00:02:08.110
and flexible with your playstyle, able to
experiment and try new things.

00:02:08.110 --> 00:02:14.000
So as you embark on your aim training journey,
keep this in the back of your mind - actively

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:19.610
improve your aim alongside the other key skills
like positioning, map awareness, decision

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:21.000
making, and so on.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:25.510
So, with that being said, what is the best
tool to improve your aim?

00:02:25.510 --> 00:02:31.970
Well, I'm sure most FPS players know what
aim trainers are.

00:02:31.970 --> 00:02:37.620
But there are still a lot of arguments as
to whether they are really that useful.

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:43.610
Many pros of the past got to where they are
without them, so should you really be using

00:02:43.610 --> 00:02:44.610
one?

00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:48.360
Well, as an ex-professional Counterstrike
player who grew up before aim trainers were

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:52.030
around, I thought it was worth it to get Ron's
opinion on this matter...

00:02:52.030 --> 00:02:57.050
RRKIM: So when they go in a game, it's like,
well when I'm playing, you're not really practicing

00:02:57.050 --> 00:02:59.610
your aim; you're practicing playing the game.

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:03.540
So you build your game sense, but you, you
know, how much aim training are you getting

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:05.900
if you're just like walking around a map not
seeing anything.

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:10.140
And there may be 10 15 seconds, or you're
just holding an angle, and there's nothing

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:11.140
happening.

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:15.300
Whereas with an aim trainer, you could in
a minute you're flicking and shooting 80-90

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:20.510
times, so you get this like instant feedback
you see where you're missing and stuff so,

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:22.880
yeah, that's the advantage.

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:27.930
For any of you guys who have taken our Esports
Elite course, you'll understand the value

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:32.620
of frequency, and this is what Ron doubles
